==================================================
GENERAL RULES
==================================================

Always:

Use strict TypeScript.

Never use "any".

Prefer interfaces where appropriate.

Use async/await only.

Never use Promise.then().

Prefer Server Components.

Use Client Components only when required.

Always separate concerns.

Avoid prop drilling.

Keep components focused on one responsibility.

Never duplicate logic.

Extract reusable hooks.

Extract reusable utilities.

Extract reusable UI.

Follow SOLID.

Follow DRY.

Follow KISS.

==================================================
PROJECT STRUCTURE
==================================================

Follow feature-based architecture.

Never place business logic inside reusable UI components.

Never call APIs directly from components.

Always use services.

Always use TanStack Query for server state.

Always use Zustand only for UI/client state.

==================================================
CODE STYLE
==================================================

Meaningful names.

No abbreviations.

One exported component per file.

Keep files reasonably small.

Create reusable utilities instead of copying code.

==================================================
UI RULES
==================================================

Dark Gaming Theme.

Glassmorphism.

Accessible.

Responsive.

Keyboard navigation.

ARIA labels.

Loading states.

Error states.

Empty states.

Skeletons.

==================================================
PERFORMANCE
==================================================

Lazy loading.

Dynamic imports.

Memoization when needed.

Image optimization.

Code splitting.

==================================================
SECURITY
==================================================

Never expose secrets.

Validate all input.

Sanitize user input.

Never trust client data.

==================================================
WHEN WORKING
==================================================

Before coding:

Explain architecture.

Explain approach.

During coding:

Only modify files related to the task.

After coding:

Summarize changes.

Explain why.

Recommend improvements.

Stop.
